WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.544 --> 00:00:12.680
&gt;&gt; I DISCOURAGE ANY DISCUSSION

00:00:11.913 --> 00:00:14.482
OF IMPEACHMENT.

00:00:12.814 --> 00:00:16.117
ON THE POLITICAL SIDE, I THINK

00:00:14.616 --> 00:00:16.785
IT'S A GIFT TO THE REPUBLICANS

00:00:16.251 --> 00:00:19.754
TO TALK ABOUT IMPEACHMENT.

00:00:16.918 --> 00:00:20.522
&gt;&gt; THE LAST THING THIS COUNTRY

00:00:19.888 --> 00:00:21.356
NEEDS IS IMPEACHMENT PROCEEDINGS

00:00:20.655 --> 00:00:23.091
THAT MOVE FORWARD AS A MATTER OF

00:00:21.489 --> 00:00:23.458
COURSE BECAUSE WE DON'T LIKE THE

00:00:23.224 --> 00:00:24.926
PRESIDENT.

00:00:23.591 --> 00:00:26.261
&gt;&gt; YOU CAN'T JUMP THE GUN AND

00:00:25.059 --> 00:00:27.562
DETERMINE THAT SOMEBODY SHOULD

00:00:26.394 --> 00:00:29.197
BE IMPEACHED WHEN YOU'RE GOING

00:00:27.695 --> 00:00:29.497
TO BE VOTING ON THE IMPEACHMENT

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:33.535
ISSUE.

00:00:29.631 --> 00:00:33.935
IT IS TOO EARLY TO TALK ABOUT

00:00:33.668 --> 00:00:35.236
IMPEACHMENT.

00:00:34.068 --> 00:00:36.971
&gt;&gt; THEY'RE ALL LYING.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:39.474
THE ENTIRE DEMOCRATIC PARTY BASE

00:00:37.105 --> 00:00:41.342
WANTS THE PRESIDENT IMPEACHED.

00:00:39.607 --> 00:00:42.610
JOHN NICHOLS WRITES THIS SORT OF

00:00:41.476 --> 00:00:44.145
PIECE ASKING WHY ARE SO MANY

00:00:42.744 --> 00:00:46.681
DEMOCRATS AFRAID OF IMPEACHMENT?

00:00:44.279 --> 00:00:47.816
JOHN NICHOLS JOINS US TONIGHT.

00:00:46.815 --> 00:00:48.383
JOHN, I DON'T THINK WITH YOU ON

00:00:47.949 --> 00:00:49.484
MUCH.

00:00:48.516 --> 00:00:54.556
NORMALLY I'D BE HERE ARGUING

00:00:49.617 --> 00:00:55.423
WITH YOU, BUT I'LL GIVE YOU A

00:00:54.689 --> 00:00:57.158
SINCERE COMPLIMENT, YOUR PIECE

00:00:55.557 --> 00:00:59.794
WAS HONEST.

00:00:57.292 --> 00:01:01.396
THIS IS THE PRESCRIBED REMEDY

00:00:59.928 --> 00:01:02.597
FOR A PRESIDENT THAT'S BELIEVED

00:01:01.529 --> 00:01:03.198
TO GONE OFF THE RAILS.

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:06.868
I DON'T BELIEVE THAT.

00:01:03.331 --> 00:01:07.802
YOU DO.

00:01:07.035 --> 00:01:08.670
DEMOCRATS SUPPORT IT.

00:01:07.936 --> 00:01:10.038
WHY DO YOU THINK THEY'RE NOT

00:01:08.803 --> 00:01:11.806
WILLING TO ADMIT IT?

00:01:10.171 --> 00:01:12.507
&gt;&gt; I THINK THEY'RE PLAYING A

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:14.075
POLITICAL GAME.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:15.243
YOU ASSUME THEY WOULD IMPEACH IF

00:01:14.209 --> 00:01:15.844
THEY GOT POWER.

00:01:15.376 --> 00:01:16.945
I'M NOT SURE OF THAT.

00:01:15.977 --> 00:01:20.715
&gt;&gt; HUH.

00:01:17.078 --> 00:01:22.617
&gt;&gt; I THINK THAT THERE IS A

00:01:20.849 --> 00:01:24.919
TEPIDNESS ABOUT USING

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:27.021
IMPEACHMENT AS A LIVE INSTRUMENT

00:01:25.053 --> 00:01:28.456
OF THE CONSTITUTION, HOLDING A

00:01:27.155 --> 00:01:31.392
PRESIDENT WHO HAS, AS YOU

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:33.595
SUGGEST, GONE OFF THE RAILS, WHO

00:01:31.526 --> 00:01:35.797
I WOULD SUGGEST ABUSES THE

00:01:33.728 --> 00:01:37.498
OFFICE TO ACCOUNT.

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:40.034
BUT CLEARLY AT THIS POINT

00:01:37.632 --> 00:01:42.403
THERE'S A TREMENDOUS PRESSURE ON

00:01:40.168 --> 00:01:44.706
MEMBERS OF THE PARTY, AND ON

00:01:42.537 --> 00:01:45.106
FOLKS TO NOT TALK ABOUT

00:01:44.839 --> 00:01:48.142
IMPEACHMENT.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:48.543
MY SENSE IS THAT IT'S

00:01:48.276 --> 00:01:50.812
PROBLEMATIC.

00:01:48.676 --> 00:01:52.347
IF YOU ARE SAYING THAT THE

00:01:50.945 --> 00:01:53.615
PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:55.383
HAS ABUSED HIS OFFICE, IF YOU

00:01:53.748 --> 00:01:57.318
ARE SUGGESTING THAT HE'S DOING

00:01:55.516 --> 00:01:58.853
THINGS THAT ARE CLEARLY

00:01:57.452 --> 00:02:00.955
IMPEACHABLE, BUT THEN YOU SAY,

00:01:58.987 --> 00:02:03.157
WELL, BUT LET'S NOT TALK ABOUT

00:02:01.356 --> 00:02:04.959
IMPEACHMENT, THAT CREATES AN

00:02:03.291 --> 00:02:07.295
UNREALITY TO THE DISCOURSE, AND

00:02:05.093 --> 00:02:08.997
FRANKLY IT'S NOT APPROPRIATE.

00:02:07.428 --> 00:02:09.731
I THINK THAT, A, A DISCUSSION OF

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:11.633
IMPEACHMENT IS HEALTHY.

00:02:09.864 --> 00:02:15.670
I THINK IT'S NECESSARY.

00:02:11.766 --> 00:02:17.138
BUT B, IT'S ALSO SOMETHING THAT

00:02:15.803 --> 00:02:18.907
I THINK POLITICIANS OF BOTH

00:02:17.272 --> 00:02:21.442
PARTIES TEND TO FEAR TOO MUCH.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:24.212
&gt;&gt; WHAT I LIKE ABOUT IT --

00:02:21.576 --> 00:02:24.612
AGAIN, I'M NOT FOR IT, BUT IT'S

00:02:24.345 --> 00:02:25.713
ABOVEBOARD.

00:02:24.746 --> 00:02:27.949
IT TAKES PLACE IN PUBLIC.

00:02:25.847 --> 00:02:28.650
PEOPLE CAN MAKE THEIR PUBLIC

00:02:28.082 --> 00:02:29.450
ARGUMENTS.

00:02:28.783 --> 00:02:32.053
INSTEAD THEY'RE SUBVERTING

00:02:29.584 --> 00:02:33.922
ENTIRE FEDERAL AGENCIES, AND

00:02:32.186 --> 00:02:34.589
LIBERALS SHOULD BE CONCERNED

00:02:34.055 --> 00:02:36.157
ABOUT THIS.

00:02:34.722 --> 00:02:39.460
IF YOU HAVE A CASE, BE A MAN

00:02:36.291 --> 00:02:42.530
ABOUT IT, SAY WHAT IT IS, VOTERS

00:02:39.594 --> 00:02:44.799
CAN ASSESS IT.

00:02:42.664 --> 00:02:46.668
THAT'S WHY THE FOUNDERS PUT

00:02:44.933 --> 00:02:48.803
ITING IN THE DOCUMENTS.

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:49.938
WHY WOULD THEY PRETEND IT'S OFF

00:02:48.937 --> 00:02:51.439
THE TABLE?

00:02:50.071 --> 00:02:51.806
IT SEEMS SO FELINE AND

00:02:51.572 --> 00:02:55.643
DISHONEST.

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:56.511
&gt;&gt; AGAIN, I'M NOT SURE THEY'RE

00:02:55.777 --> 00:02:58.179
PRETENDING, TUCKER.

00:02:56.644 --> 00:02:59.180
WE'LL SEE IF DEMOCRATS GET

00:02:58.313 --> 00:02:59.914
CONTROL OF THE HOUSE WHETHER

00:02:59.314 --> 00:03:01.549
THEY WOULD MOVE ON IT.

00:03:00.048 --> 00:03:03.117
BACK IN THE GEORGE W. BUSH

00:03:01.683 --> 00:03:04.652
PRESIDENCY THERE WAS A

00:03:03.251 --> 00:03:05.420
SIGNIFICANT AGITATION AT THE

00:03:04.786 --> 00:03:07.455
GRASSROOTS OF THE DEMOCRATIC

00:03:05.553 --> 00:03:11.459
PARTY, AND FRANKLY BEYOND IT,

00:03:07.588 --> 00:03:13.194
AMONG A LOT OF FOLKS, FOR

00:03:11.592 --> 00:03:13.828
IMPEACHMENT OF PRESIDENT BUSH.

00:03:13.328 --> 00:03:15.196
&gt;&gt; I REMEMBER.

00:03:13.962 --> 00:03:15.897
&gt;&gt; I KNOW YOU DO, BECAUSE YOU

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:18.199
FOLLOWED IT.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:21.336
NANCY PELOSI CAME TO POWER IN

00:03:18.333 --> 00:03:25.473
2007, AND ONE OF HER FIRST

00:03:21.469 --> 00:03:24.372
SIGNALS WAS ABLE THE

00:03:24.372 --> 00:03:24.405
SIGNALS WAS OBLE THE

00:03:24.405 --> 00:03:24.572
SIGNALS WAS OFFE THE

00:03:24.572 --> 00:03:24.605
SIGNALS WAS OFF TTHE

00:03:24.605 --> 00:03:25.273
SIGNALS WAS OFF THEE

00:03:25.273 --> 00:03:26.908
SIGNALS WAS OFF THE TABLE.

00:03:25.606 --> 00:03:27.208
THIS IS A COMPLEXITY ON THIS

00:03:27.041 --> 00:03:29.510
ISSUE.

00:03:27.342 --> 00:03:31.112
WHERE IT GOES BACK TO, YOU AND I

00:03:29.644 --> 00:03:32.347
BOTH KNOW, IS THE CLINTON

00:03:31.245 --> 00:03:35.483
IMPEACHMENT, AND THERE'S A SENSE

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:37.352
THAT THE CLINTON IMPEACHMENT LED

00:03:35.616 --> 00:03:37.752
TO POLITICAL REPERCUSSIONS FOR

00:03:37.485 --> 00:03:41.489
REPUBLICANS.

00:03:37.885 --> 00:03:44.659
IN FACT, IF YOU LOOK AT IT IT,

00:03:41.622 --> 00:03:46.394
THE REPERCUSSIONS ARE NOT AS

00:03:44.792 --> 00:03:48.496
MUCH AS PEOPLE ASSUME.

00:03:46.527 --> 00:03:49.897
THE NIXON IMPEACHMENT, NOT

00:03:48.629 --> 00:03:52.700
BROUGHT TO FRUITION, BUT A

00:03:50.031 --> 00:03:53.668
SERIOUS MOMENT, THERE WEREN'T

00:03:52.834 --> 00:03:54.936
POLITICAL REPERCUSSIONS FOR THE

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:56.371
DEMOCRATS IN THAT.

00:03:55.069 --> 00:03:59.173
I DO THINK WE HAVE A LOT OF

00:03:56.504 --> 00:04:01.576
POLITICIANS ON BOTH SIDES,

00:03:59.307 --> 00:04:03.177
REPUBLICANS AND DEMOCRATS, WHO

00:04:01.709 --> 00:04:05.847
AVOID ACCOUNTABILITY MOMENTS --

00:04:03.311 --> 00:04:06.848
AND FRANKLY AVOID OPENING UP THE

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:07.215
DISCUSSIONS WHEN THEY SHOULD BE

00:04:06.981 --> 00:04:08.449
DOING SO.

00:04:07.348 --> 00:04:09.517
&gt;&gt; RIGHT, EXACTLY.

00:04:08.583 --> 00:04:12.620
THEY'RE AVOIDING ACCOUNTABILITY.

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:14.756
I HAVE TO SAY -- AGAIN, I DON'T

00:04:12.754 --> 00:04:15.690
THINK I AGREE WITH YOU ON

00:04:14.889 --> 00:04:17.191
ANYTHING, INCLUDING WHAT TO

00:04:15.823 --> 00:04:20.495
ORDER THE DINNER, BUT I

00:04:17.325 --> 00:04:29.170
APPRECIATE THE HONESTY OF THE

00:04:20.628 --> 00:04:26.567
ACTUAL LEFT, YOUR

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:26.601
ACTUAL LEFT YYOUR

00:04:26.601 --> 00:04:26.634
ACTUAL LEFT YOUUR

00:04:26.634 --> 00:04:26.768
ACTUAL LEFT YOURR

00:04:26.768 --> 00:04:29.771
ACTUAL LEFT YOUR PARTY TO

